; Burrow's typed-safe storage facade over the raw LMDB FFI. Phantom transaction modes ([`R]/[`W])
; make illegal access a compile error; named sub-DBs are cached typed handles. This and burrow_lmdb
; are the only places that touch unsafe code / IO; everything above is pure values + typed handles.
; eio.unix: the durable (~8 ms F_FULLFSYNC) commit runs off the scheduler via run_in_systhread.
(library
 (name burrow_store)
 (public_name fennec-mongo.burrow.store)
 (libraries burrow_lmdb eio eio.unix))
